    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other files are support classes). BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation for owners so the app satisfies the spec and both acceptance tests pass.\n\n**Change:** `locality` is a read-only, presentation-only field on the owner response, derived from the owner's city via a fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning `UNKNOWN` for any other city.\n\n**Files edited:**\n\n1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `locality` field (with `getLocality`/`setLocality`).\n\n2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the fixed `CITY_REGION` lookup map and an `@AfterMapping` method `addLocality(...)` that sets `locality` from the owner's city (defaulting to `\"UNKNOWN\"`). This mirrors the existing pattern used for `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, and `membershipTier`.\n\nBecause `locality` is derived in the mapper, it's populated consistently on every owner response (`GET`, `POST`, list), matching how the other computed fields already work \u2014 and it required no model, service, or persistence changes.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney\u2192NSW) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city\u2192UNKNOWN) both pass; full `./mvnw test` is green.",
