    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing structure cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** `OwnerMapper` already derives a presentation-only field (`membershipTier`) via an `@AfterMapping` default method. Adding `locality` the same way follows the established in-file pattern rather than inventing a new mechanism, so a maintainer would find it natural.\n- **Table placement.** A fixed, mapper-specific lookup expressed as an interface constant (`CITY_REGION`) co-located with the one method that uses it is reasonable and self-contained; it isn't leaking domain logic into an inappropriate layer since `locality` is explicitly presentation-only.\n- **No duplication or catch-all growth.** The mapper still holds only mapping concerns (DTO conversion plus derived-field enrichment); this is another small enrichment of the same kind, not an unrelated responsibility.\n- **Additive and coherent.** The `openapi.yml` schema addition mirrors the `readOnly` derived-field convention already used for `membershipTier`, keeping the contract and mapper in step.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
